# End-to-End Capstone Project Report: Developer Technology Trends & Demographics Analysis

## Executive Summary

This report documents the end-to-end data analytics lifecycle conducted for a technology consulting organization evaluating developer preferences, tool ecosystems, compensation benchmarks, and workforce demographics. Using the Stack Overflow Developer Survey alongside labor market datasets, the objective is to extract actionable intelligence to guide enterprise software stack adoption, talent acquisition, and workforce upskilling initiatives.

The analytical workflow spans five core phases: automated data extraction (APIs and web scraping), data wrangling and anomaly mitigation, statistical exploratory data analysis (EDA), database-driven visual analysis via SQL, and interactive executive dashboard development in [Google Looker Studio](https://www.coursera.org/learn/ibm-data-analyst-capstone-project/ungradedWidget/8P7Ci/lab-26-option-b-building-a-dashboard-with-google-looker-studio).

